2025-12-14 13:25:22,905 - INFO - Generated response: Diabetic retinopathy refers to a major eye-related disorder that can occur in patients with diabetes. The disease involves the damage to retinal neurones, which leads to small vessel disease affecting the kidney's, nervous system, and retina (among other systems). This condition requires multi-disciplinary input into its care. Some of the major autonomic neuropathies associated with diabetes include postural hypotensium, gastroparesis (delayed gasemptying leading to vomiting), diaarrhoea, bladders dyshydropenia, erectile dysfunction, and stroke-like events.
